Adapted from Robust Photometric Stereo in Python, written by Yasuyuki Matsushita, Osaka University, supported by JSPS KAKENHI JP16H01732. Original README states: "This package is distributed under the GNU General Public License." No version is specified upstream; this adaptation is distributed under GNU GPL version3, whose full terms are preserved in LICENSE. Original copyright and conditions of use are retained here; exact private source revision and source notice are recorded in test/validation.md.

The bundled observations and hidden synthetic normals are existing rendered bunny assets distributed in the same original repository. They are author-provided simulations, not real photographs. Repackaging averages the existing RGB channels, preserves all50lights at native256×256, and converts original arrays to NPZ. No new synthetic acquisition is generated. Source and data attribution, changes and hashes are documented privately in test/validation.md.
